{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2151-12-01 20:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mr. ___. I'm Dr. ___, one of the surgical team members. We’ve admitted you tonight to prepare for a procedure tomorrow to help improve blood flow to your right foot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2151-12-01 20:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. The ulcers on my foot have been getting worse, and it’s been hard to walk. I’m glad we’re doing something about the circulation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2151-12-01 20:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your history of diabetes and peripheral artery disease has made it harder for wounds to heal. We’re planning an angioplasty tomorrow to open up the artery in your leg and help your foot get better blood supply."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2151-12-01 20:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had this done before, right? On the same leg?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2151-12-01 20:43:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ve had prior angioplasty and stenting. This time, we’re focusing on the anterior tibial artery, which has narrowed again. We’ll use a small balloon to open it up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2151-12-01 20:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will they use contrast dye? I remember last time my kidney function was a concern."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2151-12-01 20:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good point. We’ll use the minimal amount of contrast needed, and we’re also using CO2 to help reduce the risk to your kidneys. Nephrology is involved to make sure we protect your transplant function."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2151-12-01 20:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I’ve been taking all my meds, but my blood sugars are still high. A1c was 10.6 last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2151-12-01 20:55:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We know diabetes makes healing harder. You’re on insulin, and we’ll keep that going. The goal is to stabilize everything so your foot can heal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2151-12-01 20:58:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the ulcers? They’re not infected now, are they?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2151-12-01 21:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No signs of active infection—no fever, redness, or pus. But they’re not healing due to poor blood flow. That’s why the procedure is so important."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2151-12-01 21:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. What about my blood pressure? I noticed my chlorthalidone wasn’t on the list today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2151-12-01 21:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nephrology recommended holding the chlorthalidone for now because of your kidney transplant. We’ll restart it after your follow-up next week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2151-12-01 21:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. So no water pill until I see them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2151-12-01 21:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’re monitoring your kidney function closely. Your creatinine is stable at 1.4, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2151-12-02 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Today’s the day for your procedure. You’ll go to the angiography suite around noon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2151-12-02 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be awake?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2151-12-02 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll be under light sedation. The team will access the artery in your left groin and guide the catheter to your right leg."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2151-12-02 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Left side for access, right side for treatment?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2151-12-02 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s correct. It’s safer and easier to work from the opposite side. The procedure should take about an hour."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2151-12-02 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. The angioplasty went well. We opened the right anterior tibial artery with a 2 mm and then a 2.5 mm balloon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2151-12-02 13:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Did it work? Did the blood flow improve?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2151-12-02 13:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Before, your dorsalis pedis pulse was absent. Now it’s palpable. That’s a great sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2151-12-02 13:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good news. Any complications?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2151-12-02 13:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "None. We used only 9 cc of contrast, and your left groin site is clean with no hematoma."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2151-12-02 13:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my kidney? That’s what I worry about most."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2151-12-02 13:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your renal function remains stable. Creatinine is still 1.4. Nephrology is satisfied with how things went."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2151-12-02 13:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. What about meds now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2151-12-02 13:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll start clopidogrel today—a blood thinner to keep the artery open. You’ll take it for 30 days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2151-12-02 13:57:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Like Plavix? I’ve taken that before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2151-12-02 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, clopidogrel is Plavix. You’ll also keep taking aspirin. Don’t stop either without talking to vascular surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2151-12-02 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Understood. Can I walk?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2151-12-02 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you can walk, but avoid heavy lifting—nothing over 5 pounds—for a week to let the groin site heal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2151-12-02 14:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No lifting. Got it. And driving?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2151-12-02 14:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hold off on driving until you’re off the pain meds. Once you’re not taking oxycodone, you can resume."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2151-12-03 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re doing well. Vital signs are stable, you’re eating and walking, and your foot looks unchanged—no new issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2151-12-03 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I can go home today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2151-12-03 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We’ll discharge you. Keep elevating your leg to reduce swelling, and follow the wound care instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2151-12-03 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And when do I see the doctors again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2151-12-03 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nephrology within a week, vascular surgery in a month. Call if you have fever, new pain, bleeding from the groin, or changes in your foot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2151-12-03 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2151-12-03 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Keep up with your insulin and medications, and we’ll see you soon in clinic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2151-12-03 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One more thing—can I shower?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2151-12-03 09:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you can shower. Let the water run over the groin site, then pat it dry. No need to cover it unless there’s drainage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2151-12-03 09:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the foot ulcers?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2151-12-03 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep doing the betadine dressings as before. The improved blood flow should help them heal over time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2151-12-03 09:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do that. Thanks again, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2151-12-03 09:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, and call us if anything changes. You’re cleared to go home."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2151-12-01 20:32:00",
    "admission_end": "2151-12-03 15:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A man with a history of type 2 diabetes, kidney transplant, and peripheral artery disease was admitted for management of non-healing ulcers on his right foot. He underwent balloon angioplasty of the right anterior tibial artery to improve blood flow, which was successful as evidenced by the return of a palpable dorsalis pedis pulse. The procedure used minimal contrast to protect kidney function, and his renal values remained stable. He was started on clopidogrel for 30 days and advised to hold chlorthalidone until nephrology follow-up. He recovered well, with stable vital signs and pain control, and was discharged home with instructions for wound care, activity restrictions, and follow-up appointments with nephrology and vascular surgery.",
    "problems": [
      "Atherosclerosis of native arteries of right leg with ulceration of other part of foot",
      "Kidney transplant status",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Type 2 diabetes mellitus with foot ulcer",
      "Non-pressure chronic ulcer of other part of right foot with unspecified severity",
      "Essential (primary) hypertension",
      "Hyperlipidemia, unspecified",
      "Obstructive sleep apnea (adult) (pediatric)",
      "Other disorders of iron metabolism",
      "Long term (current) use of insulin",
      "Dependence on supplemental oxygen",
      "Peripheral vascular angioplasty status with implants and grafts",
      "Acquired absence of other right toe(s)",
      "Acquired absence of right great toe"
    ]
  }
}
